          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: holitor, holitōris",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "holitor, holitōris — \"a vegetable grower, a market gardener\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Holitor holera in forum portat et vendit. The market gardener carries vegetables to the forum and sells them."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Third declension, masculine: holitor, holitōris m., also spelled olitor. From holus 'vegetables'."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "holitor is built on holus, holeris 'vegetables, greens' with the suffix -tor 'one who' (Lewis & Short, under olitor)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
