              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "piscārius, piscāriī — \"a fishmonger\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Piscārius piscēs recentēs clāmat. The fishmonger calls out his fresh fish."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Second declension, masculine: piscārius, piscāriī m. Also an adjective: forum piscārium, the fish market."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "piscārius is built on piscis 'fish' with the suffix -ārius (EtymDB; Lewis & Short); piscis comes from PIE peysḱ-, and English fish is a Germanic cousin."
            }
          ]
        },
