          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "sporta, sportae — \"a plaited basket, a hamper\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Ancilla pānem et cāseum in sportā portat. The maid carries bread and cheese in a hamper."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "First declension, feminine: sporta, sportae f. Its diminutive sportula was the food basket, later the cash, a patron gave his clients."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "sporta is usually traced to Greek spyris 'plaited basket' (Lewis & Short compare it); EtymDB links it with PIE sper- 'to twist, to turn'. The path is not settled."
            }
          ]
        },
