              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "corbis, corbis — \"a wicker basket\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Servī ūvās in corbēs pōnunt. The slaves put the grapes into wicker baskets."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Third declension, masculine or feminine: corbis, corbis. A big basket of woven twigs, for the field or the vineyard."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "The origin of corbis is not settled: an ancient writer explained it from the bent (curvātae) twigs it is woven of, while Lewis & Short compare Greek kolpos 'fold'. EtymDB gives no parent."
            }
          ]
        },
