              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "canistrum, canistrī — \"a bread basket, a reed basket\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "In cēnā canistrum plēnum pānis est. At dinner there is a basket full of bread."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Second declension, neuter: canistrum, canistrī n., mostly plural. English canister comes from it."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "canistrum was borrowed from Greek kanastron 'basket of reeds' (EtymDB; Lewis & Short), from kanna 'reed'. English canister comes from it."
            }
          ]
        },
